.th BCHECK VIII 1976
.sh NAME
bcheck \*- read all blocks on a file system
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd bcheck
filesystem
.sh DESCRIPTION
.bd Bcheck
reads all blocks on the filesystem and if any error is encountered
attempts to correct the situation by rewriting the offending
block.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
dcheck(VIII), icheck(VIII), ncheck(VIII), check(VIII), fs(V), ipatch(VIII)
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
Gives summary of blocks on which errors were encountered.
Asks if corrective action should be taken.
Reply `y' for yes.
.sh AUTHOR
Greg Rose (University of New South Wales)
.sh BUGS
As for icheck, it believes the superblock and so can dump core.
